  "body": "### What is the issue with the Compression Standard?\n\nhttps://compression.spec.whatwg.org/#decompress-and-enqueue-a-chunk\n\n> 3. If buffer is empty, return.\n\nAnd then: \n\n> 6. If the end of the compressed input has been reached, and ds’s [context](https://compression.spec.whatwg.org/#decompressionstream-context) has not fully consumed chunk, then throw a [TypeError](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#exceptiondef-typeerror).\n\nBut this algorithm is called after the stream end is reached, step 3 would end the algorithm without throwing an error, making things invalid.\n\nWe missed this as Firefox has skipped step 3, as an empty buffer would void step 4 and 5 anyway.",
